6. Setu's look: artwork in this tree, fonts and themes in the images
   ------------------------------------------------------------------
   Artwork in this tree (docs/DESIGN.md, docs/THEMES.md), original Setu
   work under MIT OR Apache-2.0 like the rest of section 1, drawn from code
   with no third-party or Microsoft artwork; the images are made when the
   Setu image is built and are not in this tree:
     * the wallpaper collection (art/wallpapers/wallgen.py): 8 styles in
       6 palettes, installed as C:\Windows\Web\Wallpaper\Setu\*.jpg;
     * the icon sets setu-line, setu-bold, setu-duotone, setu-solid and
       setu-colour and the Setu logo variants (art/icons/icongen.py),
       installed as C:\Windows\Resources\Setu\Icons\<set>\;
     * the colour schemes (art/schemes/schemegen.py), shipped as the packs
       setu-<palette>-light and setu-<palette>-dark;
     * the cursor sets setu-light, setu-dark and setu-accent
       (art/cursors/cursorgen.py), as Windows .cur/.ani files and X cursor
       themes (/usr/share/icons/<set>);
     * the sound schemes setu-chimes, setu-wood and setu-minimal
       (art/sounds/soundgen.py), synthesized with no samples, installed as
       C:\Windows\Media\Setu\<scheme>\*.wav.

   Theme packs (distro/themes/<id>/, built by distro/themes/render-packs.py;
   each built pack carries a LICENSE file saying the same):
     * setu-light, the default pack: theme.ini, the .theme template, the
       "silk" wallpaper (artwork/wallpaper.py), the Setu bridge mark, the
       installer's Calamares images and the boot splash images
       (artwork/branding.py), and the Plymouth theme, Calamares style sheet
       and labwc theme templates (boot/, installer/, linux/): original Setu
       work, MIT OR Apache-2.0. Its icons are the setu-colour set, its
       cursors the setu-light set and its sounds setu-chimes (above). Text
       in its images is set in Inter (below); a picture of text is not font
       software, and no font file is in this tree.
     * setu-dark: theme.ini only (everything else comes from setu-light),
       with the wallpaper ridges-setu-dark of the collection and the
       setu-dark cursors: original Setu work, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
     * setu-<palette>-<light|dark> (12 packs): schemegen's theme.ini with
       Base=setu-light or setu-dark and a collection wallpaper: original
       Setu work, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
     * In every pack, visual/<id>.msstyles is the Setu control theme
       (below; LGPL-2.1-or-later), and the fonts are Debian's (below).

   Third-party artwork in this tree:
     * Lucide icons: see section 5.
     * The Setu control theme (personality/wine/dlls/setu.msstyles),
